    "title": "pandas.tseries.holiday.previous_friday — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1663.g6eba694f5d documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.tseries.holiday.previous_friday#\n\n- \npandas.tseries.holiday.previous_friday(*dt* )[source]#\n- Move Saturday and Sunday back to the previous Friday. A holiday on a weekday keeps its date. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **dt** datetime\n    - The date the holiday falls on.\n  - Returns:\n    - datetime\n    - The date the holiday is observed on.\n See also \n  - `tseries.holiday.next_monday`\n  - Move Saturday and Sunday to the following Monday.\n  - `tseries.holiday.previous_workday`\n  - Move to the previous weekday.\n  - `tseries.holiday.Holiday`\n  - Class that defines a holiday with start/end dates and rules for observance.\n Examples >>> from datetime import datetime >>> from pandas.tseries.holiday import previous_friday >>> previous_friday(datetime(2022, 1, 1)) # Saturday datetime.datetime(2021, 12, 31, 0, 0) >>> previous_friday(datetime(2022, 1, 2)) # Sunday datetime.datetime(2021, 12, 31, 0, 0)",
    "markdown_length": 903,
